        "summary":  "Google launched Gemini 3.7 Flash at approximately 50% lower pricing than its predecessor ΓÇö $0.75 per million input tokens and $3.75 per million output tokens ΓÇö positioning it as a \u0027workhorse model for coding and agents\u0027 with significant benchmark improvements. The release reflects Google\u0027s strategy of accelerating Flash model updates while slowing the Pro tier cadence, signaling a bifurcation between high-frequency, cost-optimized inference and frontier capability development. Industry analysts note this pricing compression makes production-scale agent workflows more economically feasible, but warn that differentiation increasingly depends on governance infrastructure and orchestration layers.",
        "execSummary":  "Google\u0027s 50% Flash price cut is the clearest signal yet that the unit economics of enterprise AI inference are entering a deflationary phase ΓÇö what was cost-prohibitive at scale six months ago is now viable. For enterprise technology leaders, this is the moment to revisit AI deployment business cases that were shelved due to inference cost projections: the numbers have materially changed. The strategic caveat from analysts is important: as model prices converge downward across providers, the competitive advantage will increasingly come from governance, orchestration, and integration depth ΓÇö not raw model performance. Organizations that have invested in building strong AI operations foundations will be positioned to capture the value of cheaper inference faster than competitors.",
        "vendorLean":  "Google",
