        "execSummary":  "Enterprise leaders should note that Microsoft\u0027s FY26 report positions agentic AI governance ΓÇö not just deployment ΓÇö as the differentiator separating high-performing organizations from experimenters. Customers running 10,000+ agents (Atos at 19,000) are achieving 20-68% efficiency gains in specific workflows, signaling that scale requires unified governance platforms, not ad hoc tools. For customer-support leaders, the Navien case (28,000 annual hours saved) and Chow Tai Fook (57% sales conversion lift via agents) show the support-to-sales continuum is being redrawn by agentic AI. The key caveat: Microsoft is defining the governance frameworks customers run on, creating significant platform lock-in risk that procurement leaders should factor into multi-year contracts.",
