        "summary":  "AWS demonstrates a three-tier agentic architecture combining self-hosted models on Amazon SageMaker AI with managed foundation models through Amazon Bedrock AgentCore, where an orchestrator agent routes tasks to either a budget agent or a financial analysis agent running Qwen 3.5 9B on SageMaker. The article addresses a critical observability gap: Bedrock automatically instruments model calls with token telemetry, but SageMaker endpoints require manually emitting OpenTelemetry spans to capture equivalent usage data. The guide covers authentication patterns, streaming configuration, and production deployment to AgentCore runtime.",
