        "theme":  "Agents",
        "summary":  "AWS provides a step-by-step implementation guide for integrating autonomous payment capabilities into OpenClaw agents using Bedrock AgentCore Payments and the x402 protocol. The architecture separates human-controlled payment policy administration (approved recipients, spending limits, asset types) from agent execution, so the model cannot create or exceed pre-approved payment sessions. The guide includes wallet provisioning through Coinbase or Stripe, policy configuration, and test deployment on Base Sepolia testnet.",
        "execSummary":  "This developer guide operationalizes the AgentCore Payments GA announcement and reveals the actual security model: rather than preventing prompt injection attacks on payment-capable agents, the architecture assumes compromise is possible and bounds the blast radius through layered policy controls ΓÇö IAM role separation, recipient whitelists, per-transaction ceilings, and session expiration. This is a pragmatic but important design philosophy for enterprise security teams to evaluate: the system is designed to contain damage, not prevent all unauthorized action. For AI operations leaders deploying customer-facing agents with spend authority, the policy separation pattern described here should become a required architectural standard. The testnet deployment path signals this is still early-stage technology where production hardening will matter.",
