        "summary":  "NVIDIA Nemotron 3 Ultra achieved the highest accuracy among open models on LangChain\u0027s Deep Agents benchmark while operating at 10x lower inference cost per run than leading closed models, with the performance gains coming from system prompt and tool description optimization rather than model retraining. NVIDIA released NemoClaw, an open reference blueprint combining the tuned agent code with NVIDIA OpenShell\u0027s secure runtime for enterprise deployment. Companies including Abridge, Amdocs, Box, and EY are implementing specialized agents on this stack for business-critical workflows.",
        "execSummary":  "The benchmark result reframes the open vs. closed model debate for enterprise AI buyers: Nemotron 3 Ultra matches frontier closed-model accuracy on agent tasks at a fraction of the cost, and the performance came from harness engineering rather than model improvements ΓÇö meaning enterprises can apply the same optimization methodology to their own deployments. For AI strategy leaders, the 10x cost differential at comparable accuracy is a material input to build-vs.-buy decisions, particularly for high-volume agent workflows where inference costs compound quickly. The NemoClaw open reference stack also signals NVIDIA\u0027s intent to compete on the full agent deployment layer, not just accelerator hardware. The key caveat is that benchmark performance on LangChain\u0027s harness may not transfer directly to domain-specific enterprise workflows, so internal validation against production tasks remains essential before switching from closed to open models.",
