        "theme":  "Platforms",
        "summary":  "Snowflake launched dynamic model routing for its Cortex AI Gateway, automatically directing AI workloads to appropriate models based on cost, performance, and latency policies. Internal testing showed up to 3x greater token efficiency compared to using frontier models exclusively for all tasks. Industry experts caution that enterprises must factor in implementation complexity, governance overhead, and additional troubleshooting variables when evaluating the net cost benefit.",
        "execSummary":  "Snowflake\u0027s dynamic model routing is a direct response to enterprise cost anxiety around AI inference spend, automatically steering workloads to less expensive models when full frontier-model capability is unnecessary. For CIOs managing AI budgets, this represents a meaningful platform-level lever to contain costs without sacrificing capability on high-value tasks. The strategic implication is that AI gateways are becoming a critical layer in enterprise architecture, routing intelligently rather than defaulting to the most powerful model every time. However, the added routing layer introduces new governance and debugging complexity that IT teams must account for in total cost of ownership calculations.",
